  "result": "Subcommands now get their defaults from the `default_map` entry matching their name, so `default_map` values set for a subcommand are no longer ignored. The full test suite passes (1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Changes**\n- **`src/click/core.py`:** the subcommand context now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)` instead of the parent's whole mapping. If there's no entry for the subcommand, it gets no default map, as before.\n- **`tests/test_defaults.py`:** three new tests:\n  - a subcommand reads its value from `default_map`, and a CLI argument still overrides it;\n  - a subcommand with no matching entry falls back to its parameter default;\n  - a nested group resolves defaults by name at each level.\n- **`CHANGES.md`:** an \"Unreleased\" entry describing the fix.\n\n**Verification**\n- With the fix reverted, the two subcommand tests fail, so they catch the bug. With the fix in place, all three pass.\n- The fix is restored in `core.py`; the revert was only temporary.\n\nI haven't committed anything. If you want a commit, tell me and I'll create one.",
